{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2115","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Gellyfish and Flaming Peony"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Gellyfish hates math problems, but she has to finish her math homework:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Gellyfish is given an array of $$$n$$$ positive integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"She needs to do the following two-step operation until all elements of $$$a$$$ are equal:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Select two indexes $$$i$$$, $$$j$$$ satisfying $$$1 \\leq i, j \\leq n$$$ and $$$i \\neq j$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Replace $$$a_i$$$ with $$$\\gcd(a_i, a_j)$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now, Gellyfish asks you for the minimum number of operations to achieve her goal."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It can be proven that Gellyfish can always achieve her goal."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 5000$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq n \\leq 5000$$$) — the length of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\leq a_i \\leq 5000$$$) — the elements of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$5000$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer — the minimum number of operations to achieve her goal."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n3\n12 20 30\n6\n1 9 1 9 8 1\n3\n6 14 15\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n3\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, the following is a way that minimizes the number of operations: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose $$$i = 3$$$ and $$$j=2$$$ and replace $$$a_3$$$ with $$$\\gcd(a_3,a_2) = \\gcd(30, 20) = 10$$$, then $$$a$$$ becomes $$$[12, 20, 10]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose $$$i=1$$$ and $$$j=3$$$ and replace $$$a_1$$$ with $$$\\gcd(a_1,a_3) = \\gcd(12, 10) = 2$$$, then $$$a$$$ becomes $$$[2, 20, 10]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose $$$i=2$$$ and $$$j=1$$$ and replace $$$a_2$$$ with $$$\\gcd(a_2,a_1) = \\gcd(20, 2) = 2$$$, then $$$a$$$ becomes $$$[2, 2, 10]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose $$$i=3$$$ and $$$j=1$$$ and replace $$$a_3$$$ with $$$\\gcd(a_3,a_1) = \\gcd(10, 2) = 2$$$, then $$$a$$$ becomes $$$[2, 2, 2]$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"2115A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2115/problem/A"}